WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:48.460
Let's see who wants to check in today.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.739
Let's go to Chris from Texas.

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:50.739
Chris from Texas.

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:51.739
You were on.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:53.940
What is on your mind today, my friend?

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.100
Hey, David.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.100
Can you hear me?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.010
I can hear you perfectly, all right.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:03.420
I called you about a couple of months ago
and I wanted to say thank you for, like.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.610
Teaching me how to think more critically,
like I remember saying how I could fight that

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.860
battle with other people, when you're looking
at the polls from 538.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.570
It looks like it's pretty much over for Trump
at this point.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:20.500
I mean, Biden would have to have to literally
about have to die in order for Trump to win

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.500
right now.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.750
Well, listen, I hope that you are right, but
all we need to do is just vote, right.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.100
We ultimately have no control over anything
other than whether we vote.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.240
So I love the optimism.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.610
The polls look ugly right now, but we just
don't know.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.350
In the 25 days that are left, we just don't
know.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.220
So I share your cautious optimism.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.810
Let's focus on the cautious and let's make
sure we vote.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.490
Yeah, I understand.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.490
I'm going to vote.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.990
I'm going to vote next week.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:52.380
Tuesday as well.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.509
Beautiful.

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:54.640
Also.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.119
So also wondering to now, like with two of
the Senate members testing positive different

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.399
Corona virus, three, in fact.

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:01.690
Oh, three three now.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:05.060
Yeah, well, it's it's Mike Lee.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.060
Thom Tillis and Ron Johnson.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.060
Yeah.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.869
So you think it's possible that Amy Coheed.

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:12.250
How you pronounce your name.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.650
Amy CONI Barret's nomination will be the lead
now.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:20.600
I do think that there is a good chance that
it doesn't happen before Election Day.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:25.670
But if Republicans are determined, I don't
see any way that it won't happen during the

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.350
period between the election and the inauguration.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:35.120
My only hope is if the corona virus positives
prevent the vote from happening before November

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:41.850
3rd and then Joe Biden wins and Democrats
take the Senate and the Martha McSally seat

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.239
is immediately seated because remember, that's
a special election.

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:48.290
So, Mark, if Mark Kelly wins, he might be
seated right away.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:54.430
I'm hoping that there would be such outrage
if Republicans still try to push it through.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.920
I'm talking outrage to the point of mass rallies,
and I don't know if that will happen.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.769
That would be the dream scenario that Republicans
abandon the nomination.

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:05.500
It's very optimistic.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.750
It's very uphill.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.060
But I think it's the only chance we've got.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.820
Also, I'm kind of worried about packing the
courts as well.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:16.500
I thought, I know people say that they want
to pack the courts just because they want

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.250
to at least be able to get progressive reform.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.250
Yeah.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.489
But I'm worried that it could be used against
us in the future for Republicans to pack the

00:03:22.489 --> 00:03:23.489
court as well.

00:03:23.489 --> 00:03:24.530
It certainly could.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.750
But here's the here's what I would say.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.459
Here's what I would say to that, Chris.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:33.160
Joe Biden has has not answered whether he
would or wouldn't be in favor of that.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.209
And I think he's been smart not to answer
it for now because it would.

00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:38.049
Whatever he answers will become the focus.

00:03:38.049 --> 00:03:39.949
And it's not really what this is about.

00:03:39.949 --> 00:03:44.540
If you look back at Joe Biden's history, my
reading of it is that he is unlikely to pack

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.540
the court.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.010
So I actually if you're concerned about that,
I don't actually think Biden will do it.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.010
Okay.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:54.120
My last question is, what do you think we
should do if Joe Biden becomes president?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:58.960
Shall we try to push for more leftwing policies
or should we just try to undo all of the damage

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.130
Trump has done first?

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.130
Well, it's both.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.130
It's not one or the other.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:06.540
I mean, a lot of the damage Trump has done
can be undone via executive orders that give

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.540
orders.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:11.769
And at the same time, particularly if Democrats
take the Senate, then you've got big legislative

00:04:11.769 --> 00:04:13.730
accomplishments that we can start working
on.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:14.730
So you've got to do both.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.730
Yes.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.730
All right.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.820
Thank you for the time, David.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.329
Chris, I appreciate it so much.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:20.459
Chris from Texas.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:05:40.069
Great to hear from Chris from Texas.

